  "response_text": "The stack pool is the segment of memory where all of the threads stacks are stored. The allotted stack memory can be divided between multiple threads, so that they each have their own individual stack that they can use.\\nThis is useful because it allows stacks to essentially have a memory workspace where they don\u2019t have to worry about it being overwritten or modified by other processes or when they are not currently executing any instructions. Furthermore, if each thread stack is the same size, then a given thread\u2019s stack pointer offset can be easily computer by multiplying the thread number by the thread stack size, and adding the stack size for that thread.\\n",
